# Tomik, Distinguished Advokist: "Your opponents can't play land cards from graveyards" (CR 101.2, 305.1), which takes
# precedence over Crucible of Worlds' permission (the card's ruling). Both players crack a Marsh Flats and have a Crucible.
# On turn 3 Bot1, Tomik's controller and no opponent of its own, plays its Flats from its graveyard. On turn 4 Bot2 can't
# play its Flats from its graveyard, its land play still unused, and plays an Island from its hand. Once Tomik dies to a
# Lightning Bolt, on turn 6, Bot2's Crucible lets it play the Flats from its graveyard.

